WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:02.550
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.220
- There really is a
before and after Sephora,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.430
when it comes to the makeup industry.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.140
- [Narrator] Until about 20 years ago,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.020
this is how most Americans
shopped for luxury makeup.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.430
A sales representative of the brand

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.400
would stand behind the makeup counter

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.460
and help customers make a purchase.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.320
- That completely changed with Sephora.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.050
Now it's a free for all,
people walk in the stores,

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.780
they test whatever they want,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.910
nothing is behind the glass.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.200
- [Narrator] So, how
did this French retailer

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.360
come to dominate the global personal care

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.010
and beauty product industry

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.970
and what business practices helped make it

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.033
the industry leader that it is today?

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.363
This is the Economics of Sephora.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.560
Today, the beauty retailer
employs over 36,000 people

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:52.060
in more than 2,700 stores,
in over 35 countries.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.200
Those stores carry over 250 beauty brands.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.406
- [Man] At this point,

00:00:57.406 --> 00:00:59.480
Sephora's like kind of my second home.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.940
- [Narrator] The Sephora that
we know today has its roots

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.180
in a small perfume shop
that opened in 1969

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.970
in Limoges, France.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.440
At that time, the perfume
and cosmetics market

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.550
was dominated by a
service-based retail model

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.680
in which staff typically
received commissions

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.200
based on sales.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.750
Instead, Sephora used the
assisted self service model,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.660
in which customers are free
to test products in the store.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.190
- You have a full where you can just

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.750
like literally grab whatever

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.340
and you can try on the lipsticks,

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.340
you can try in the eye shadows.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.450
I always leave looking like
a literal different person

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.660
than I arrive.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.428
- [Narrator] Sephora customers
can still request help

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:37.660
from a sales associate who
Sephora calls a beauty advisor.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.500
- A little bit more trust
with the sales representatives

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.480
in a Sephora store, because
they're brand agnostic.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.810
So they can tell you,

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.460
maybe you should buy the
mascara from this brand,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.490
but you should buy the blush
from a different brand.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.190
- [Narrator] Sephora
also bucked convention

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.070
in the manner in which it
displayed its products.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.750
- [Woman] So make-up items
are next to each other.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.810
Whereas from the same brand,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.910
a fragrance would be
in the fragrance aisle.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:02.910
From the same brand,

00:02:04.555 --> 00:02:06.025
a skincare product would
be in the skincare isle.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.870
- [Narrator] Then in 1997,
founder Dominique Mandonnaud

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:11.710
sold Sephora to the large luxury
retail conglomerate, LVMH.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.520
- One of the advantages of being owned

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.810
by a conglomerate like LVMH,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.550
is that the company can
jump very quickly on trends.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:22.610
And actually, several of
the brands that are sold

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.360
in Sephora stores are owned by LVMH.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.670
- [Narrator] One of the
popular brands owned by LVMH

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.550
is Fenty Beauty by Rihanna.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.100
- [Woman 2] And then Fenty
of course has a huge section.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.870
The whole row of Fenty, we
got the lip glosses up front.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.610
- [Narrator] Sephora's success also stems

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.860
from its exclusive line of products.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.050
- There's a little bit of a tension

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.720
in the relationship between
a store and a brand.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.830
Because Sephora is such a hot store

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.099
for makeup brands to
sell their products in,

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:52.360
Sephora ends up having a lot more leverage

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.660
in that relationship.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.140
- [Woman 3] The Sephora collection.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.100
- [Woman] The challenge
for high-end beauty brands

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.370
these days is that they're
really facing a conundrum.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.450
They've become increasingly
dependent on Sephora

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.250
for sales growth, but because LVMH

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.670
also produces beauty brands

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.580
and there's an element
of competition there,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.810
and more brands are coming out constantly.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.050
The shelf space is shrinking.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.910
- [Woman 4] Five Sephora
products you need to try part 10.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:18.450
- [Narrator] In part due to
that product exclusivity,

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.800
Sephora boasts a loyal customer base.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.260
- Here are five Sephora products
you need to buy tonight.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.110
Sorry, I don't make the
rules you just have to.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.560
- So what you'll find oftentimes
on Instagram or TikTok,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.700
is that people have these haul videos

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.650
where they're showing all
the products that they bought

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.090
in Sephora, and they're going one by one,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.000
talking about them.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.440
- [Man] This is the KOSAS
tinted face oil, and it's $42.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.050
I recommend this product to everyone

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.080
and they're always like I'm paying $42

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.910
for a face oil, yes you are.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.300
- [Narrator] Many faithful customers

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.080
are members of Sephora's
Beauty Insider program,

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.600
which has three different tiers

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.080
and more than 25 million members.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:56.060
The lowest tier is the Beauty Insider.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.140
The next level up is VIB, or
Very Important Beauty Insider,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:04.610
which users must spend $350
in a calendar year to unlock.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.940
The top level is called Rouge,
which customers can access

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.200
after spending at least
$1000 in a calendar year.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.210
Benefits like savings
increase with each tier.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:17.360
- I'm Rouge, don't judge me,
I know I spend a lot of money.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.337
Okay, I get it.

00:04:18.337 --> 00:04:19.890
- But the real advantage for Sephora

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.490
for the beauty rewards
program is that every time

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.760
a customer goes in there,

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.110
Sephora knows exactly what they bought.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:29.724
And that is very valuable
information for the company

00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:32.440
to understand who the customer is,

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.100
what they're purchasing
and then down the road,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.270
be able to market in a
very personalized way

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.320
to that customer.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.910
- [Narrator] Yet as much
as the company profits

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.430
on exclusivity with its products,

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.870
when it comes to Sephora's consumer base,

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:47.010
the retailer takes inclusivity seriously.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.180
- One of the ways that
Sephora has tried to become

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.580
more inclusive is by featuring
a larger number of brands

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.840
in their stores, they've made an effort

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.370
to include black owned brands,

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.280
and then also by pushing brands

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.110
to expand their product
lines and offer products

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.240
that appeal to people from
different racial groups,

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.880
different ethnicities.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.430
- [Narrator] In 2021,
Sephora relaunched Color IQ,

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.400
a skin tone matching technology.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.530
The company offers to assist customers

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.820
in selecting the most natural
products for their skin tone.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.230
- [Woman 5] All the products
that would be your exact color.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.320
- [Narrator] And Sephora
is still expanding.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.240
In December 2020, the company
announced a partnership

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.030
with the department chain Kohl's,

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:31.030
to install 850 shops inside
Kohl's stores by 2023.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.730
Since opening 200 Kohl's
locations this summer,

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:37.380
Sephora has added 200,000
new Beauty Insiders.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.010
in a statement to the Wall Street Journal,

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.320
a Sephora spokesperson said,
we want to be an unequivocal

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.800
global leader in the prestige beauty space

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.450
and a purpose driven brand

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.210
that is a transformative
opportunity for everyone we touch.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.970
They continued by
outlining three main areas,

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.350
customers, brands and teams.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.060
- Sometimes when customers step outside

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.160
of the Sephora store,
they will have splotches

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.680
of makeup all over their arms.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.260
And that really showcases

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.976
what they've been doing in this store.

00:06:03.976 --> 00:06:06.559
(gentle music)

